Rationale: The claim has three material parts: (1) the author of 'What is Property?' was a member of a national governing body, (2) he inspired a political group founded by George Valois and Georges Sorel, and (3) Olivier Ferrand was elected to the governing body. The first part is not supported by any evidence, as multiple searches for which governing body Proudhon was a member returned INSUFFICIENT. The second part is also INSUFFICIENT, as no evidence connects Proudhon to Valois or Sorel. The third part is unrelated to the first two and is not addressed in the evidence. Further investigation is needed to confirm or refute these claims.
